# nverts [4 4] parses and allocates fine; verts's third entry, 2.5, is not
# an integer, so TokenVector::toRtIntVector() throws mid-array. The already-
# built nverts array must not leak across that throw. This is a genuine
# token-level syntax error (RIE_SYNTAX), not one of this request's own
# softer structural checks, so it aborts the file: unlike the other
# malformed fixtures here, the trailing Sphere is never reached.
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
AttributeBegin
	PointsPolygons [4 4] [0 1 2.5 3 4 5 6 7]
		"P" [-1 -1 0  1 -1 0  1 1 0  -1 1 0
		     -0.4 -0.4 0  -0.4 0.4 0  0.4 0.4 0  0.4 -0.4 0]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
	Translate 2 0 0
	Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
